annotations('UploadRepository.kt',{
20:'Hilt injects the application Context, avoiding storage of an Activity. The repository uses it to open content URIs.',21:'Starts class-level constants.',22:'Sets the HTTPS host of the dummy API; no Firebase token is sent to this endpoint.',25:'Declares a suspend upload operation returning UploadReceipt. withContext(IO) moves blocking file/network work off the main thread.',26:'Checks experiment-ID syntax and description limits again, independently of the UI.',27:'Opens the selected content URI through ContentResolver. use closes the image stream when finished.',28:'Collects the bounded file bytes in memory; this is not a bitmap or decoded pixel array.',29:'Allocates an 8192-byte buffer for reading the source stream.',30:'Reads repeatedly until the image stream ends.',31:'Stops cooperative file-reading work if the upload coroutine has been cancelled.',32:'Reads the next chunk and records the actual byte count.',33:'A negative byte count means end-of-stream; leave the loop.',34:'Rejects the read before adding a chunk that would exceed 5 MiB. Exactly 5 MiB is accepted despite the wording "smaller than".',35:'Copies only the bytes read, not the unused portion of the buffer.',37:'Produces the byte array that will form the multipart image part.',38:'Throws a readable error when ContentResolver cannot supply an input stream.',39:'Configures an image-bounds-only decode so validation does not allocate the full image pixel buffer.',40:'Inspects the image bytes to populate dimensions and detected media type.',41:'Reads the decoder-detected MIME type rather than trusting a filename extension.',42:'Accepts JPEG and PNG; rejects HEIC, GIF and other image types for this server contract.',43:'Rejects a file whose image dimensions cannot be decoded.',44:'Generates a random multipart boundary separating form sections. This UUID is not a retry/idempotency event ID.',45:'Opens the API URL as an HTTP connection. Because the URL uses HTTPS, transport uses TLS.',46:'Starts a block whose finally clause will release the connection on success or failure.',47:'Uses the POST operation advertised by the OpenAPI specification.',48:'Allows up to 90 seconds to establish the connection, including potential server startup delay.',49:'Allows up to 90 seconds for a blocking response read; this is not a guaranteed total request deadline.',50:'Does not automatically follow redirects, so the multipart payload is not silently forwarded to another URL.',51:'Allows writing a request body.',52:'Requests a JSON response through the Accept header.',53:'Declares multipart/form-data and the exact boundary used below.',54:'Builds the text headers and fields that come before the raw image bytes.',55:'Adds the experiment_id form part. Literal \\r\\n sequences in source become CRLF separators in the HTTP body.',56:'Adds the description form part as UTF-8 text.',57:'Adds the image part disposition with a generated filename and extension matching the detected MIME type.',58:'Adds the image media type and a blank CRLF line before the binary image data.',59:'Encodes multipart text as UTF-8 bytes.',60:'Builds the closing multipart boundary after the image bytes.',61:'Declares the exact request-body length so HttpURLConnection can stream a fixed-size body.',62:'Checks for cancellation before starting the request write.',63:'Writes form headers/text, image bytes, then the final boundary. use closes the request output stream.',64:'Reads the HTTP status code, waiting for the response if necessary.',65:'Treats only 2xx responses as success.',66:'Converts known HTTP error statuses into readable IOException messages.',67:'Maps 413 to the server image-size rejection.',68:'Maps 415 to unsupported/invalid image content.',69:'Maps 422 to missing or invalid form fields.',70:'Reports the status code for any other error, including redirects and 5xx responses.',73:'Reads the successful response as UTF-8, closes its stream, and parses it with Android JSONObject.',74:'Checks that this is the expected stub response with connection_ok status. Other modes require an intentional client update.',75:'Provides the failure message when the response is not the connectivity-test format.',77:'Opens the nested image receipt JSON object.',78:'Constructs the strongly named response model returned to the ViewModel.',79:'Reads required request ID, experiment ID and description fields; getString throws when required data is missing.',80:'Reads the server message, image media type and received byte count.',81:'Reads width, height and server SHA-256 to complete the receipt.',83:'Runs cleanup regardless of the return value or exception.',84:'Releases the HttpURLConnection. Cancellation cannot guarantee that the server did not already receive the upload.'})
