p('Choose an experiment, choose or capture an image, enter a description, then tap Continue. The app uploads the data and opens a conversation-style response screen. It shows loading, the submitted image/text, an actual server message and image receipt. Retry resubmits a failed upload. Exit conversation and system Back return Home, clear the image/description, and retain the selected experiment.')
h('Important boundary')
p('No follow-up message API, experiment-list API, event/version contract, restoration endpoint or server-side close operation was present in the inspected deployment. The app does not invent those endpoints or generate fake circuit verdicts. The request ID in the receipt is not a restorable session ID.')

section('1. Integration steps in implementation order')
steps=[('1 - Inspect the service','Read /openapi.json and GET /health. Discover the actual /api/sessions path, required form fields, supported image formats, size limit and StubResponse shape.'),('2 - Verify a real request','Send a synthetic 16 x 16 PNG to the live endpoint. Confirm connection_ok and the echoed experiment/image receipt before writing the Android request.'),('3 - Define the client models','Add UploadReceipt and UploadRules. Represent the fields Android needs and reject invalid IDs/descriptions.'),('4 - Build the upload boundary','Add UploadRepository. Read a bounded URI stream, inspect image metadata, create the multipart body, post over HTTPS, handle HTTP statuses and parse the receipt.'),('5 - Add conversation state','Add ConversationUiState and ConversationViewModel. Track one draft, loading, result and error; preserve the draft for manual Retry.'),('6 - Render the response','Add ConversationScreen with the submitted image/description, loading indicator, server receipt, errors, Retry and Exit.'),('7 - Add a route','Add ScreenRoute.Conversation and declare its Navigation 3 entry in MainActivity.'),('8 - Wire Continue','Add the callback through HomeDestination. MainActivity captures the selected experiment and Home draft, starts the upload and pushes Conversation.'),('9 - Enforce form requirements','Update HomeScreen so description is required and limited to 2000 String units before Continue is enabled. Image format/size is checked in the repository.'),('10 - Exit and clear','Cancel client work, clear conversation and Home draft, pop back to Home. Do not clear the selected experiment.'),('11 - Verify and document','Run assembleDebug and testDebugUnitTest, add UploadRules tests, and write the runbook. Device UI testing remains a separate check.')]
simple_table([['Step','What was done']]+steps,[160,590])

section('2. The real request and response contract')
p('The inspected dummy service uses one multipart upload endpoint, not the larger proposed sessions/events design discussed earlier.')
simple_table([['Request part','Meaning and constraint'],['experiment_id','Required ID: 1-100 ASCII letters, digits, underscores or hyphens. The app currently sends local IDs such as ohms-law.'],['description','Required text. The app trims the draft before sending and rejects blank or more than 2000 Kotlin String units.'],['image','Required JPEG or PNG file, at most 5 MiB (5,242,880 bytes).'],['Transport','HTTPS POST to /api/sessions with multipart/form-data and an explicit boundary. No Firebase token or version field is attached.']], [160,590])
simple_table([['Response field','How Android uses it'],['mode / status','Requires stub and connection_ok to accept the response.'],['request_id','Shown for debugging one request; not used to restore a conversation.'],['experiment_id / description','Stored as echoed form values. The screen uses the draft description and displays the echoed experiment ID.'],['message','Displayed exactly as the server explanation.'],['image','Contains content_type, size_bytes, width, height and sha256. The UI displays dimensions, bytes and hash.'],['ml1 / ml2','Not parsed into diagnosis UI because they are stubs.'],['413 / 415 / 422','Mapped to image size, invalid image and invalid form messages respectively.']], [160,590])
h('Reading multipart code')
p('A boundary is a unique separator between fields. Content-Disposition identifies each part by its form name. The text \\r\\n in Kotlin strings becomes HTTP CRLF separators. The body is built as: text fields and image headers + raw image bytes + closing boundary. A file extension is chosen from the decoded media type, not a user-provided filename.')

