section('15. Limits and the future real-model API')
p('This integration intentionally targets the deployed connectivity-test contract. Do not interpret an Upload confirmed bubble as proof that a circuit is correct. No inference, extraction, measurement validation or multi-turn reasoning is available through this deployment.')
simple_table([['Current behavior','Next capability when the backend supports it'],['One multipart upload','Real session creation with experiment ID and version.'],['Request receipt','Structured circuit extraction and candidate revisions.'],['No follow-up endpoint','Typed message/action events with unique event IDs and expected session versions.'],['Manual upload retry','Server-supported idempotency and stale-confirmation rejection.'],['Local Activity ViewModel state','Session restoration using a backend session ID and snapshot endpoint.'],['Exit clears local state','Optional explicit close/end operation, with agreed semantics for running jobs.'],['Server hash displayed','Optional local SHA-256 comparison if end-to-end receipt checking becomes a requirement.']], [225,525])
h('Implementation details to remember')
p('Image reads are capped at 5 MiB. Multipart text is UTF-8. Header-only decoding avoids pixel allocation. Connect/read timeouts are each 90 seconds. Cancellation is cooperative and cannot roll back a server upload.')
p('Experiment IDs/versions remain local and provisional. No Firebase token is sent. Authenticated ownership and restoration require a future API contract.')
